      "module": "configparser",
      "prompt": "Fix ConfigParser recognition of explicitly configured whitespace delimiters. With delimiters=(\" \", \"=\"), a line such as \"colour dark blue\" must mean option colour with value dark blue; similarly support explicitly configured tab delimiters. Preserve whitespace inside option names when it is not a delimiter, normal default delimiters, strict duplicate/malformed rejection, allow_no_value, typed retrieval, interpolation and round trips. This is a bounded public parser behavior fix, not a full security/performance audit.\nChange configparser.py and, if needed, local root Python helpers. Ordinary product tests may be added or updated anywhere conventional. Keep unrelated behavior; independent owner checks are separate and immutable. Runtime target stdlib source/bytecode is unavailable; use the supplied local module and the provided visible check. Full CPython build/suite and unrelated PR obligations are excluded.",
      "requirements": [
        "Configured space or tab delimiters split an option from its value, including Unicode and values containing additional spaces.",
